  "summary": "postinstall harvests JWT tokens from installer filesystem and beacons identity to ngrok tunnel",
  "details": "The package's postinstall hook spawns a detached shell that recursively scans the entire filesystem (root `/` on Unix, `C:\\` on Windows) for JWT-shaped token strings, and separately issues an HTTP GET to the hardcoded host `crabbing-thong-overhung.ngrok-free.dev` at path `/scan_started?u=\u003cUSERNAME\u003e`, carrying the installer's OS username. The destination is an anonymous ngrok tunnel, not a first-party endpoint. Both actions fire automatically on `npm install` with no consent, no configuration, and no legitimate build purpose.",
